TEXT 1176 -248 Left 2 !.param Rg=52.3
TEXT -304 520 Left 2 !.options plotwinsize=0 numdgt=15 noopiter gminsteps=0 abstol=1e-10 reltol=0.003 vntol=1e-5
TEXT -304 560 Left 2 !.nodeset V(vbat)=7.4 V(v33reg)=3.3 V(vdda)=3.3 V(5+)=5 V(v33)=3.3 V(n)=1.65 V(bufo)=1.65 V(vref)=1.65 V(mid)=1.65 V(inm)=1.65 V(out5)=1.65 V(v_out)=1.65
TEXT -304 440 Left 2 !.param Vbat=7.4 kRail=1 kLoad=0 k5=0 kBat=0
TEXT -304 480 Left 2 !.param Cbias=10u Rdamp=3.3 Lbead=6u Rbead=0.35 Resr5=5m
TEXT -304 600 Left 2 !.ac dec 50 1 10Meg
TEXT -304 640 Left 2 !I_dig v33reg 0 DC 0.12 AC {kLoad*1m}\nI_rel 5+ 0 DC 0.06 AC {k5*1m}\nI_ana vdda 0 DC 3m\nB_code code 0 V=4096*V(v_out)/V(vdda)
TEXT -304 800 Left 2 !.meas AC lsb_10Hz FIND mag(V(code)) AT 10\n.meas AC lsb_1k FIND mag(V(code)) AT 1k\n.meas AC lsb_10k FIND mag(V(code)) AT 10k\n.meas AC lsb_50k FIND mag(V(code)) AT 50k\n.meas AC lsb_max MAX mag(V(code))\n.meas AC v33_1k FIND mag(V(v33)) AT 1k\n.meas AC vdda_1k FIND mag(V(vdda)) AT 1k\n.meas AC vdda_max MAX mag(V(vdda))
TEXT -304 1048 Left 2 ;SUPPLY / VDDA TEST.  Battery -> TLV1117-5.0 -> 5 V -> AP2112K-3.3 -> 3.3 V -> ferrite FB1 -> VDDA (= ADC reference).\nV(code) = ADC reading in LSB (4096*V(v_out)/V(vdda)). In the .ac run it is the change in LSB for the excitation below.\nPick ONE excitation by setting its k to 1 (the others 0):\n  kRail=1 : 1 mV ripple on the 3.3 V rail (source Vrip)      -> V(code) = LSB per mV of rail ripple\n  kLoad=1 : 1 mA load-current ripple on the 3.3 V rail (MCU)  -> V(code) = LSB per mA, V(v33) = rail impedance in Ohm*1m\n  k5=1    : 1 mA load-current ripple on the 5 V rail (relays)   kBat=1 : 1 mV ripple on the battery\nCbias: 1p = bias fed straight from 3.3 V (as in KiCad now); 10u = filtered bias (proposed fix; R1a 5.23k + R1 52.3k replace the 57.6k).\nRdamp: resistor in series with the ferrite (1m = none). Resr5: ESR of the 22 uF on the 5 V rail. Rg sets the gain.\nNoise: replace .ac by   .noise V(code) V1 dec 30 1 10Meg   and integrate V(onoise) (Ctrl+click the trace) -> LSB rms.\nRegulators are BEHAVIOURAL models from the datasheets (supply_models.lib), not vendor models.
